  Dittner and Hartke (2018) report converged charges of about
  -0.11 e and +0.09 e. At those magnitudes the term is far below
  the resolution limit of roughly 0.6 kcal/mol that the
  single-charge test established, so contributions may be summed.
  The failure of additivity measured at unit charge does not
  transfer to the magnitudes a design would use.

